## Business OS (`.ai.biz/`) — business strategy and execution

**Cohabitation:** this block coexists with the other OS frameworks registered in this file. Business work writes only under `.work.biz/`. It never edits `.work/`, `.work.ui/`, another framework's section of this file, or application code without saying so and asking first in the same message.

REPLACE_BIZ_POINTER_SECTION

### Source resolution and path rules

Apply these before reading any `.ai.biz/<path>` reference in this block:

1. `.cursorrules` (this file) and `.work.biz/**` — always local, in both modes.
2. **Thin-client** (`$AI_BIZ_SOURCE` set and readable): every other `.ai.biz/<path>` resolves to `$AI_BIZ_SOURCE/<path>` — `skills/<id>/skill.md`, `skills/SKILL_DEPENDENCIES.md`, `standards/**`, `concepts/**`, `docs/**`, `scripts/**`, `templates/**`. Never assume a local `.ai.biz/` exists.
3. **Fat-client**: read `.ai.biz/<path>` locally in this repo.
4. **Unreachable source:** stop and report `business-os source unreachable: $AI_BIZ_SOURCE`. Do not fall back to a local `.ai.biz/` and do not guess another path.
5. Other frameworks' roots are resolved by their own sections. Never resolve a `.ai/` or `.ai.ui/` path from this block.

**Sibling frameworks:** the cross-framework registry lives in `$AI_BIZ_SOURCE/.cursorrules` § Frameworks registry — its path cells are host-specific. A sister that is not installed routes as `[degraded: <framework> not installed]`; never route into the void.

