### Change safety (business work)

| Gate | Command | Fail when |
|------|---------|-----------|
| Touch scope | bash scripts/touch-scope-verify.sh | File outside `.work.biz/touch-scope` |
| Blast radius | bash scripts/blast-radius-check.sh | Cross-area diff ≥3 areas |
| Gate check | bash scripts/gate-verify.sh | A gate claims PASS without its evidence |
| Framework verify | bash scripts/framework-verify.sh | Non-zero exit |

**Declare scope first:** copy `$AI_BIZ_SOURCE/templates/work/touch-scope.template` → `.work.biz/touch-scope`.

### Business gates

| Gate | Evidence | Promoted by |
|------|----------|-------------|
| `strategy-ready` | `.work.biz/strategy/certification.md` | `@biz-strategy certify` |
| `brand-ready` | `.work.biz/reference/BRAND_STATUS.md` | `@biz-brand overhaul` |
| `pipeline-ready` | `strategy/pricing.md` + pipeline tracker + outreach cadence | `@biz-review status` |
| `sales-ready` | Pipeline tracker with a logged discovery call | `@biz-discovery run` |
| `active-deal` | Pipeline tracker with a live deal | `@biz-discovery run` |

**Reading rule:** a gate is met only when its `**Status:**` line in `.work.biz/gates.md` starts with `PASS`. Never infer a gate from the presence of files.

### Business protected files

Do not modify unless the operator explicitly asks in the same message: `skills/SKILL_DEPENDENCIES.md`, `standards/`, `hooks/`, `templates/`, and the Business OS block in this file. (Application-level protected files listed by other frameworks still apply.)

### Output contracts (binding)

- **Operator handoff** — close every operator-facing report per `$AI_BIZ_SOURCE/skills/SKILL_DEPENDENCIES.md` § Operator handoff contract: terse output; `**Needs your approval:**` numbered with `path:L<n>` cites; `**Needs your answer:**` numbered and never mixed with approvals; exactly one `**Next step:**`; Form A single line when nothing is needed; empty sections omitted.
- **Document clarity** — every generated document carries a ≤4-line Status/Needs header, separate Decisions / Open questions lists, exactly one `## Next action`, and no leftover scaffolding.
- **Evidence discipline** — any market claim carries a citation or an explicit `directional` / `Unverified` marker, plus an evidence grade `A`–`D` when the claim carries a decision. Model memory alone may never carry one.

### Business documentation conventions

Strategy documents live under `.work.biz/strategy/`; plans `plan_<topic>.md` under `.work.biz/plans/`; research `research_<topic>.md`; drafts `draft_<topic>.md`. Dated documents use a `YYYYMMDD-` prefix. No "Generated by" lines, no agent signatures, no dates-as-signatures.

